-- S23 Maharashtra prose — morgaon
-- Verdict matrix: 8 go / 1 skip / 3 wait
-- Anchors: Mayureshwar — FIRST + LAST Ashtavinayak in traditional yatra, Sage Mudgala establishment, Karha river, svayambhu peacock-Ganesh murti with Nagaraj cobra above + lion vahana, Pune 64km via Saswad/Jejuri, Bhuleshwar nearby

INSERT INTO destination_months (
  destination_id, month, verdict, score, prose_lead, why_go, why_not
) VALUES
('morgaon', 1, 'go', 4, 'January at Morgaon — the FIRST and LAST temple in the traditional Ashtavinayak yatra order — runs at clean post-festival operational tempo. Mayureshwar, the peacock-mounted form of Ganesha (mayura is Marathi for peacock — the village derives its name), sits on the Karha river bank 64km southeast of Pune via Saswad and Jejuri. The svayambhu (self-manifested) murti carries the distinctive cobra-canopy iconography — Nagaraj rising above the head — and uniquely names the lion as its vahana rather than the standard mooshik (mouse). Sage Mudgala is credited with establishing the temple in its current form. Daytime 16-29C, nights 10-12C — among the year-cleanest temple weather. Standard darshan 5am-10pm with mid-morning palki processions. Sankashti Chaturthi falls early month bringing standard Tuesday density. The 64km drive from Pune takes 90 minutes via Hadapsar-Saswad route; combine with Bhuleshwar (45km) for a clean day-trip. Morgaon village stays modest — pilgrim lodgings ₹400-1,200, Saswad/Jejuri-side hotels ₹1,200-2,500.', 'January 16-29C and clean post-festival calm. Mayureshwar svayambhu peacock-Ganesh with Nagaraj cobra above + lion vahana on full schedule. 64km Pune drive 90 min via Saswad-Jejuri. Pilgrim lodging ₹400-1,200, combine with Bhuleshwar.', NULL),
('morgaon', 2, 'go', 5, 'February makes Morgaon a Maghi Ganesh Jayanti centerpiece. The festival — Magh Shukla Chaturthi — falls Wednesday 4 February 2026, and as the FIRST + LAST temple in the Ashtavinayak yatra (pilgrims start and end here in the traditional sequence), Morgaon attracts the heaviest single-temple density of the secondary yatra peak. The svayambhu Mayureshwar murti — with the Nagaraj cobra rising above the head and the unusual lion vahana iconography — receives the pre-dawn maha-abhishek ritual; palki processions run mid-morning and evening. Angarki Chaturthi falls Tuesday Feb 3 — the day before Jayanti, compounding pilgrim density. Daytime 17-31C, nights 11-13C — near-perfect temple weather. The 64km drive from Pune takes 2 hours on festival days through Saswad-Jejuri traffic. Pilgrim lodgings book three weeks ahead at ₹600-1,500 festival rates. Bhuleshwar 45km away handles the overflow accommodation. Sage Mudgala lineage Vaishnavite pilgrims arrive from Andhra and Tamil Nadu through the festival window.', 'Maghi Ganesh Jayanti Wed Feb 4 + Angarki Chaturthi Tue Feb 3 at the FIRST + LAST Ashtavinayak. Heaviest secondary-peak density. Pre-dawn maha-abhishek, palki processions. Lodgings ₹600-1,500, book 3 weeks ahead.', NULL),
('morgaon', 3, 'go', 4, 'March holds Morgaon at clean operational temperature through the first three weeks with the Marathi New Year cultural pull mid-month. Gudi Padwa — falls Thursday 19 March 2026 — brings extended morning ritual schedule at Mayureshwar and pilgrim traffic from the wider Pune Marathi community. Daytime 21-34C, nights 15-17C; the Karha river runs at low pre-monsoon flow visible from the temple ghat. The svayambhu Mayureshwar murti receives standard 5am-10pm darshan; the peacock-Ganesh with its distinctive cobra-canopy and lion-vahana iconography sits at full ritual tempo. Sankashti Chaturthi mid-month brings dedicated Tuesday pilgrim density. By final week the heat ramp starts to bite — mid-day temple courtyard becomes uncomfortable. The 64km Pune-Saswad-Jejuri drive remains 90 minutes on weekdays; weekend traffic adds 20 minutes. Pilgrim lodgings hold at ₹500-1,200. Last clean-comfort window before April pushes the temple into compressed-hours operation.', 'Gudi Padwa Mar 19 — Marathi New Year extended morning ritual at Mayureshwar. 21-34C through first three weeks. Karha river at low flow. Sankashti Chaturthi mid-month. Last clean window before April heat.', NULL),
('morgaon', 4, 'wait', 3, 'April pushes Morgaon into heat-compromise territory. Daytime 26-39C on the Pune plateau; the temple courtyard stone holds heat 8am-7pm. The svayambhu Mayureshwar darshan remains operational but compresses to pre-9am and post-5pm windows. The peacock-Ganesh murti with its Nagaraj cobra canopy and lion vahana sits at full schedule but the pradakshina circuit (the open courtyard around the temple) becomes uncomfortably hot by 10am. Karha river at lowest pre-monsoon flow — the ghat stays workable but the wider riverbed dries to dust. The 64km Pune drive is the most uncomfortable stretch; AC-bus packages from Pune drop to ₹450-700 per pilgrim. Pilgrim arrivals thin sharply through month; lodging rates drop to ₹400-900. The committed pilgrim flow (Sage Mudgala lineage Vaishnavites from south India) shifts to dawn-only darshans. Temple cool stone interior holds 33-35C — better than outside but not comfortable. Push to October for the post-monsoon ideal window.', 'April compresses to pre-9am and post-5pm darshans. 26-39C; pradakshina circuit uncomfortable past 10am. Karha river at lowest flow. Pune AC-bus ₹450-700. Pilgrim flow thins. Push to October.', 'April runs at fragmented schedule. 26-39C heat compresses Mayureshwar darshan to dawn and dusk windows; pradakshina circuit uncomfortable past 10am. The full temple experience does not happen. Push to October.'),
('morgaon', 5, 'skip', 2, 'May is unviable Morgaon. Daytime 30-42C on the Pune plateau — among the hottest stretches in central Maharashtra; the temple stone courtyard hits 50C surface temperatures by noon and holds heat through midnight. The svayambhu Mayureshwar darshan continues but the practical pilgrim experience collapses — even the 5am dawn slot opens at 28C and reaches 35C by closing. The peacock-Ganesh murti with the Nagaraj-cobra and lion-vahana iconography sits in the cool stone interior (33-35C through day) but the open-air pradakshina circuit and the Karha river ghat approach are physically punishing. Karha river at year-low flow — the riverbed dusty. The 64km Pune drive in an AC bus tolerable; the temple visit itself is the failure point. Angarki Chaturthi falls Tuesday 5 May 2026 — dedicated pilgrim flow continues but most committed yatra-pilgrims skip Morgaon through May. Lodgings drop to ₹400-800 deep off-season. Push to October.', NULL, 'May 30-42C — among hottest central-Maharashtra stretches. Temple courtyard stone 50C surface noon. Even 5am dawn slot opens at 28C and reaches 35C. The full Mayureshwar darshan experience collapses to a fragmented dawn fragment. Push to October.'),
('morgaon', 6, 'wait', 3, 'June marks southwest monsoon arrival in Morgaon. First-week rains break the heat — daytime 22-32C, nights 19-21C. The Karha river starts to swell visibly through month; by final week the ghat steps below the temple begin to flood. The svayambhu Mayureshwar darshan continues at standard 5am-10pm schedule — the temple sits well above the river bank — but the temple-side ghat approach becomes weather-dependent in the last two weeks. The peacock-Ganesh and its Nagaraj-cobra iconography under a fresh post-rain green Pune-plateau setting is among the better viewing conditions of the year. The 64km Pune drive can take 2 hours through monsoon delays on the Saswad ghat section. Sankashti Chaturthi falls late month; pilgrim flow modest. Pilgrim lodging ₹500-1,200 with monsoon discount. Time the visit to morning windows after the previous night rain has cleared; expect at least one wet darshan stretch.', 'June monsoon arrival — 22-32C, post-rain green Pune plateau, fresh visual context for Mayureshwar peacock-Ganesh. Karha river starts to swell. 64km Pune drive may take 2 hours with monsoon delays.', 'June transitions the landscape but adds operational drag. Karha river begins to swell — ghat approach weather-dependent in last two weeks. Saswad-ghat drive delays add up to 30 minutes; expect at least one wet darshan stretch.'),
('morgaon', 7, 'wait', 3, 'July holds monsoon-peak rainfall on the Pune plateau — Morgaon receives 350-500mm through the month. The Karha river overflows the lower ghat steps reliably through July; the temple platform remains dry (the structure sits well above the riverbed) but the lower ghat approach becomes unusable on heavy-rain days. The svayambhu Mayureshwar darshan continues at reduced morning-only schedule on monsoon days. The peacock-Ganesh with the Nagaraj-cobra and lion-vahana iconography in its lush rain-soaked context is photographically striking but operationally compromised. The 64km Pune drive takes 2-2.5 hours through Saswad ghat caution. AC-bus packages drop to ₹450-700; private operator services suspended on weather-watch days. Sankashti Chaturthi pilgrim flow continues but at modest density. Lodgings drop to ₹400-1,000 at deep monsoon rates. Combine with Bhuleshwar visit only if the morning rain has cleared — both temples sit close enough to align weather windows.', 'July rain-soaked peacock-Ganesh visual context, but Karha river overflows lower ghat, Saswad drive 2-2.5 hours through monsoon caution. AC-bus packages cut to ₹450-700. Morning-only darshan reliable.', 'July monsoon peak — Karha river overflows lower ghat steps through month; temple platform dry but ghat approach unusable on heavy-rain days. AC-bus services on weather-watch suspension. The reliable yatra experience does not happen.'),
('morgaon', 8, 'wait', 3, 'August continues monsoon peak but adds the first major pilgrim anchor since June. Angarki Chaturthi — the Tuesday-Sankashti combination — falls Tuesday 4 August 2026, drawing committed pilgrim flow despite the rain. Morgaon sees a 50 percent traffic increase on the Tuesday and Wednesday around the festival. The svayambhu Mayureshwar with its Nagaraj-cobra and lion-vahana iconography runs extended ritual schedule for the festival; the temple platform remains dry but the Karha river still overflows the lower ghat. Daytime 22-31C, humid; rainfall sustained through month at 300-400mm. The 64km Pune drive on Saswad ghat takes 2-2.5 hours through caution sections. Pilgrim density picks up through final week as the Ganesh Chaturthi build approaches — the September festival is just two weeks out and pre-festival pilgrim flow starts arriving. Lodgings rise to ₹500-1,200 from the early-month deep discount.', 'August Angarki Chaturthi Tue Aug 4 brings committed pilgrim flow despite rain. Mayureshwar peacock-Ganesh on extended Tuesday-Wednesday ritual. Pre-Ganesh-Chaturthi build through final week. Lodgings ₹500-1,200.', 'August holds monsoon peak with operational uncertainty — Saswad ghat 2-2.5 hours, Karha river still overflows lower ghat. Most pilgrim arrivals concentrate on Aug 4-5 festival window; the rest of the month remains weather-dependent.'),
('morgaon', 9, 'go', 5, 'September makes Morgaon the absolute Ashtavinayak yatra peak — and as the FIRST and LAST temple in the traditional pilgrimage order, this is where pilgrims begin and end their circuit. Ganesh Chaturthi (Bhadrapada Shukla Chaturthi) falls Saturday 12 September 2026 — the 10-day festival running through Anant Chaturdashi Tuesday 22 September 2026. The svayambhu Mayureshwar receives continuous palki processions, special pre-dawn maha-abhishek every morning, full puran-poli and ukadiche-modak prasad distribution. Dindi pilgrim groups arrive from across Maharashtra. The 10-day window operates at festival saturation. Daytime 22-30C with monsoon tail rains through first week tapering by Anant Chaturdashi. The 64km Pune drive runs at 2-2.5 hours through festival traffic; private operators run 3-day Ashtavinayak packages ₹6,500-8,000 starting and ending at Morgaon. Lodgings book out 90 days ahead at festival rates ₹1,500-3,500. Karha river at clean post-monsoon flow with the ghat approach fully restored.', 'Ganesh Chaturthi Sep 12-22 — FIRST + LAST Ashtavinayak at festival saturation. Continuous palki processions, special pre-dawn abhishek, puran-poli prasad. Lodgings ₹1,500-3,500 festival rates, book 90 days ahead.', NULL),
('morgaon', 10, 'go', 5, 'October is post-monsoon ideal Morgaon. The 10-day Ganesh Chaturthi peak has dispersed; through the first two weeks the residue pilgrim density continues at strong tempo, then by mid-month settles into clean operational tempo at the freshest visual context of the year. Daytime 19-32C, nights 16-18C — among the year-cleanest temple weather. Karha river at full post-monsoon flow; the temple ghat platform fully restored, water visible from the courtyard. The svayambhu Mayureshwar with its Nagaraj-cobra canopy and lion vahana sits against a green Pune-plateau backdrop at peak photographic clarity. Angarki Chaturthi falls Tuesday 6 October 2026 bringing dedicated pilgrim density without the September overload. The 64km Pune drive returns to 90-minute standard time. Lodgings drop to ₹500-1,500. Combine with Bhuleshwar 45km for a clean day-trip; the post-monsoon route through Saswad and Jejuri runs at year-best visual condition.', 'Post-monsoon ideal — 19-32C, Karha river at full flow, temple ghat fully restored. Mayureshwar peacock-Ganesh + Nagaraj-cobra + lion-vahana iconography at peak photographic clarity. Angarki Chaturthi Tue Oct 6. Combine with Bhuleshwar.', NULL),
('morgaon', 11, 'go', 5, 'November is the year-best Morgaon. The post-monsoon Pune-plateau green still holds through first two weeks; daytime 16-30C, nights 12-14C — the sharpest cool weather of the year. The svayambhu Mayureshwar darshan at full 5am-10pm schedule with light woolens needed for the 5am slot. The peacock-Ganesh murti with the Nagaraj-cobra canopy and lion-vahana iconography sits in its cleanest visual presentation of the year. Karha river at clean post-monsoon flow; the temple ghat fully restored. Sankashti Chaturthi mid-month brings standard Tuesday density. The 64km Pune drive runs cleanest of the year — 85-90 minutes on weekday mornings, surface condition of the Saswad ghat at its annual best after the monsoon-repair cycle. Pilgrim lodgings ₹500-1,500 at standard rates. Pune escape weekend traffic from Friday afternoon onward is the only operational caveat — book Sunday-Tuesday for the cleanest experience.', 'November year-best — 16-30C, sharpest cool of year, Mayureshwar peacock-Ganesh at cleanest visual presentation. Karha river clean. Saswad ghat surface at annual best. Sun-Tue cleanest, avoid Fri-Sun escape traffic.', NULL),
('morgaon', 12, 'go', 4, 'December at Morgaon opens with Angarki Chaturthi — Tuesday 1 December 2026, the auspicious month-opener pulling dedicated pilgrim flow. The svayambhu Mayureshwar runs full ritual schedule with strong first-week density. Daytime 14-29C, nights 9-11C — the coolest stretch of the year. Light woolens essential for 5am dawn slot. The peacock-Ganesh murti and its Nagaraj-cobra canopy + lion-vahana iconography against the cool dry Pune-plateau setting at clean visual presentation. Karha river at moderate flow. The 64km Pune drive runs heavy weekend traffic through the Pune-tourist-escape season — 15 percent longer through December weekends. Sankashti Chaturthi mid-month brings standard Tuesday flow. Pilgrim lodgings rise to ₹600-1,700 at year-end tourist peak. Pune-escape weekenders compete with pilgrim flow on the Saswad-Jejuri road; the last week (Dec 25-31) at heaviest traffic density. Book mid-month weekdays for cleanest operational experience.', 'Dec 1 Angarki Chaturthi opens strong. 14-29C, year-coolest. Mayureshwar peacock-Ganesh clean visual presentation. Light woolens for 5am slot. Lodgings ₹600-1,700. Book mid-month weekdays to avoid Pune-escape traffic.', NULL)
ON CONFLICT (destination_id, month) DO UPDATE SET
  verdict = EXCLUDED.verdict,
  score = EXCLUDED.score,
  prose_lead = EXCLUDED.prose_lead,
  why_go = EXCLUDED.why_go,
  why_not = EXCLUDED.why_not;
